    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "ति ॥ सावधानः स्यात् ॥ चान्यन्मन्दमन्दं पदं रचयति योजयते ॥ कथं (sic. again)",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "लोकचित्तानुवृत्त्या. Were it not that the construction of कृत्वा, or त्यक्त्वा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "as we have it, has been otherwise stated in this commentary, it",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "would be unnecessary to point out that the correct construction",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "is अपशब्दं च दूरतस्त्यक्त्वा...निरतो भवति.—Mandâkrântâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XI.—प्रमाणीकृतम् = प्रमाणोपेतं कृतमित्यर्थः (commentary in M.)",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "which itself requires explanation. प्राप्यत्वेन निर्णीतम् (Râmarshi) which is better. It means “settled as one's measure i. e. as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "one's proportion or share” उपनमेत् is better than उपनयेत् in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "sense of “will go to” as in इदमुपनतमेवं रूपमक्लिष्टकान्ति in S'âkuntala.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "उपनयेत् the commentator in M. explains by ढौ (sic. ढौ ?) कयेत्प्राप्नो-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "तीत्यर्थः. But this is avoiding the difficulty. Both उपनयेत् and ढौकयेत्,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "unlike प्राप्नोति (which is a correct rendering for उपनमेत् ), require",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "a subject who should cause to go. This subject it is difficult to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "find except by the awkward way of supplying दैवम्. On the other",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "reading तत् would be the subject not the object as here. महानाश्रयः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "धनाद्यधिकरणम् says Râmarshi; resort to a high place &c. आशा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "quarters, directions, द्वित्राः = two or three. Pâṇini V., 4, 73.—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "Region r4 cut-out misses line 3 ('which is better...') and the ends of lines; transcribed from full page image, placing the missed line at the end of n=2."
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XII.—The reading वा does not make sense. नो for न would",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "suit both sense and metre. स्वैरकथा ordinary random conversa-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "tion. Comp. Vîracharita 4 (Trith.).—Âryâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XIII.—कन्दुकपातेन पतति is a curious construction “falls with",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the fall of a ball” i. e. so as to rebound. The construction of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "second line is also curious. Râmarshi's comment runs as follows:",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "आर्यः श्रेष्ठः पुमान्प्रायः बाहुल्येन स्वभावेन वा पतन्नपि विपदं प्राप्नुवन्नपि उत्पतति ऊर्ध्वं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "गच्छति संपदं प्राप्नोतीत्यर्थः ॥ केन तुल्यं कन्दुकपातेन सह कन्दुकपातवत् । यथा कन्दुकः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "पतन्नुत्पतति । तु पुनः अनार्यः खलस्तथा पतति भ्रस्य (sic. इय) ति तथा कथं यथा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "मृत्पिण्डपतनं मृदः मृत्तिकायाः पिण्डः सार्द्ररजःसंघातः तस्य पतनं यथा भवति न तु कदा-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "चिदुत्पतनं भवेत्.—Anushṭubh.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "Region r6 cut-out misses the last line ('चिदुत्पतनं भवेत्.—Anushṭubh.') and the ends of lines; placed the last line in n=8."
    },
